WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.859
Britain says it will issue thousands of emergency
visas to foreign truck drivers to help ease

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:11.660
supply chain problems that have led to fuel
rationing and empty shelves at supermarkets.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:17.160
In the aftermath of Brexit, thousands of foreign
drivers left the U-K, since they could no

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.090
longer work visa-free.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.800
And now ordinary Britons are feeling the effects.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.699
Chaos at the petrol station.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:33.740
Despite government pleas NOT to panic buy
fuel, long queues have built up at the pumps.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.780
A shortage in lorry drivers has led to delivery
bottlenecks across the UK,

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.199
forcing some stations to close or to ration
what fuel they have left.

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:49.629
A nightmare for those who depend on the fuel
for work.

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:52.640
It's stupidity that we're all queuing up.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.379
But this is my job, so I have to have diesel.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:00:58.379
That's it.

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:00.829
I'm in here for my work.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:02.629
I never know where it's going.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.230
So I've got to have diesel.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.239
Look at my tank.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:08.320
I don't fill up usually, I leave it.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.420
But look at that, it's empty.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.009
How am I going to get to work on Monday?

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:14.750
You with me?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.920
I'm done.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.829
I've been to three stations.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:24.479
Analysts say the driver shortages were caused
by the pandemic and Brexit.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:29.659
Various sectors had previously warned that
supplies would run short.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:34.710
Many supermarket shelves have been left empty
for weeks.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:40.729
The UK government, facing growing pressure,
has now announced a temporary visa scheme

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:45.920
for 10,500 lorry drivers and poultry workers.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.900
But this will hardly be enough to ease the
pressure.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:57.369
Estimates suggest the UK is short of about
100,000 heavy goods vehicle drivers.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:01.450
"I think we need is a bit of political pragmatism
here.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.950
We`ve got an absolute crisis in the supply
chain facing us.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:10.190
Of course there are political principles involved
in this, but there's also the principle of

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.160
making sure that people in Britain get their
food and their fuel."

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.050
Frustration among citizens is growing, too.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.330
"This is Brexit personified.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
-- Why is that?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.630
-- No truck drivers.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:32.630
All the foreign nationals who are Europeans
have left the country because of Brexit."

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.310
And with Christmas around the corner, the
situation could get even worse.

